      "text": "Ten feet twenty, the Flower Man\nIs waiting for the touch of his hand\nStraightening petals out without a plan\nLike the ever daily\nWish that bothers the Flower Man\nCould I do something to make him laugh?\nInside my little chamber made of glass\nSo he lives the\nFlower Man, Flower Man\nWith his heart in the sand\nSo he stands\nTo watch the whole wide world\nFrom a can\nWay up high in the sky\nWith the sun in his eyes\nAin't it nice?\nThe life forever for\nFlowers\nLong as we flowers hold any power\nWe'll use it for our king of flowers\nNever again!\nWill we have to watch him sigh\nUnder this running sky\nHopes and dreams\nAre they fantasies?\nIf they're no more than dreams\nThen let us dream\nLet me dream!\nJust a fantasy?\nCause they feel real to me\nIf that's all you can dream\nThen let him dream!\nAre they hopes or dreams?\nAre they how we cope? (And nothing more)\nIf they're no more than hopes\nDon't let us know\nLet me hope!\nIn this fantasy\nI can clearly see him happy\nThough it's make-believe\nIt's what he needs!\nTen feet twenty, the Flower Man\nIs waiting for the touch of his hand\nFallen to pieces still without a plan\nYet the ever daily\nHope that powered the Flower Man\nWould never cower off of its path\nEven if broken I am more than glass!\nSo he lived the\nFlower Man, Flower Man\nWith his heart in the sand\nSo he stands\nTo watch the whole wide world\nFrom a can!\nWay up high in the sky\nWith the sun in your eyes!\nAin't it nice?\nThe life forever for\nFlowers",
